425
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:53,890
<i>Are Time Machines Possible?</i>

426
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:53,840
Thank you all for coming here today.

427
00:02:55,550 --> 00:03:00,300
I don't have much experience with lectures like these.

428
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:01,760
So I hope you'll bear with me.

429
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:05,100
Makise Kurisu's giving the lecture...

430
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,480
So she isn't a ghost?

431
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,690
Still talking about that?

432
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:13,400
I've been asked to speak to you about time machines.

433
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:17,860
It's a different theme than that of my <i>Science Magazine </i>essay,

434
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:20,320
but I'd like to give it a try.

435
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:22,070
Time machines?

436
00:03:22,070 --> 00:03:30,040
I believe that time machines are foolishness.

437
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:33,840
I'd like to spend the lecture discussing how I arrived at that conclusio â

438
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,130
Objection!

439
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,590
Time machines are impossible?

440
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:41,050
It's far too early to decide that!

441
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:43,010
Okarin, you're embarrassing yourself.

442
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:44,430
You're...

443
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:53,150
I believe that "early" isn't the issue.

444
00:03:53,150 --> 00:03:55,440
It's theoretically impossible.

445
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,940
What?

446
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:02,700
Well then, let's change the format of this lecture to a discussion.

447
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:06,700
That will make it easier for certain stubborn people to understand.

448
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:10,040
Right? Hououin Kyouma-san?

449
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:24,010
Makise Kurisu...

450
00:04:24,010 --> 00:04:25,550
And from this,

451
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:27,930
we can conclude that, in a string theory-based universe,

452
00:04:27,930 --> 00:04:29,640
time travel is unrealistic.

453
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:31,440
You want to try it?

454
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:33,400
Hououin-san?

455
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:36,900
I imagine so...

456
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:40,530
Then why not find some exotic matter for us,

457
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,320
Hououin-san?

458
00:04:44,410 --> 00:04:49,870
That's all I have to say. But if you have further objections, I'm listening.

459
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:51,460
Hououin-san!

460
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:56,290
Don't be so damned arrogant, 
just because you've some little bit of genius!

461
00:04:56,290 --> 00:05:00,760
Wait... She must be an Organization agent.

